{
  "path": "lua/common/filters.lua",
  "module": "Collection of stateful numeric filters (smoothing, low-pass/high-pass, spring, frequency detector, linear regression) used throughout the vehicle code (pedal/steering inputs, sensors, controllers). Each filter is created by a global function newXxx(...) that returns an object with a get(sample, dt) method (or get(sample) for fixed-step filters) that updates the internal state and returns the filtered value. The constructors are global variables: `require('filters')` is not necessary once the module is loaded (loaded by default in both VMs).",
  "usage": "local smoother = newTemporalSmoothing(5, 5)          -- 5 units/s when rising and falling\nfunction updateGFX(dt)\n  local out = smoother:get(rawInput, dt)\nend\n\nlocal lp = newFreqFilter1()\nlocal y = lp:getLowPassFreq(sample, dt, 10) -- 10 Hz low-pass",
  "notes": [
    "This file does not return a table M: everything is global (freqGenC, newFreqFilter1, newFreqDetector, newFreqExists, newTemporalSpring, newTemporalSigmoidSmoothing, newTemporalSmoothingHybrid, newTemporalSmoothingNonLinear, newTemporalSmoothing, newLinearSmoothing, newNopSmoothing, newExponentialSmoothing, newExponentialSmoothingT, newLineFitting). The classes (metatables) are local and only accessible through the created objects.",
    "IMPORTANT: the snippets of the auto page give signatures without the sample (e.g. get(dt)). In the code, the sample is ALWAYS the first argument after self: get(sample, dt), getLowPassFreq(sample, dt, cutOffFreq), lineFitting:getS(x, y), lineFitting:get(x, y, dt), etc.",
    "Input/output rate filters (temporalSmoothing, temporalSmoothingNonLinear, temporalSmoothingHybrid, temporalSigmoidSmoothing, linearSmoothing): the object stores two rates in the boolean keys [false] = inRate and [true] = outRate. At each step, the key used is (sample - state) * state >= 0: so when the difference has the same sign as the state (the value moves away from 0, or the state is 0), the rate stored in [true] (= outRate) applies; when the value comes back toward 0, it is [false] (= inRate). This is the code's behavior, regardless of the parameter names.",
    "temporalSmoothing is LINEAR (speed bounded to rate units/s), temporalSmoothingNonLinear is EXPONENTIAL (st += dif * rate*dt/(1+rate*dt)), temporalSmoothingHybrid = exponential with a minimum speed linearRate. Infinite input rates are brought to 1e30 (NonLinear, Hybrid) or the lower bound to 1e-307 (Linear).",
    "temporalSmoothing:getCapped/getWithRateCapped bound the output to [-1, 1]; getUncapped = get (alias) and getWithRateUncapped = getWithRate (alias). If autoCenterRate (3rd constructor argument) differs from inRate, getUncapped becomes getUncappedAutoCenter; getCapped goes through getUncapped, so auto-centering is only active via getCapped/getUncapped, not via get().",
    "newExponentialSmoothing: the internal constant is computed with fixedDt (0.0005 s by default); the window is expressed as a number of samples (minimum 2). Do not use it with a variable time step (use getWindow or a temporal filter).",
    "lineFitting: samples x, y; weight = slope, bias = intercept. window is in samples for getS, in seconds for get. For numerical stability, scale the inputs to [0,1] or [-1,1] (code note). If scale <= 0 or nil, scale = 1000. lineFitting:set(window, ...) only sets decay with the sample-based formula (1 - 2/(window+1)), but get() recomputes decay on each call.",
    "freqExists:get / getS / bufferStart-bufferAdd-bufferEnd implement the Goertzel algorithm to measure the amplitude of a given frequency in a signal.",
    "In the code, getUncapped is referenced in temporalSmoothing:getCapped but is only defined by alias after the class definition (temporalSmoothing.getUncapped = temporalSmoothing.get): OK.",
    "temporalSigmoidSmoothing and temporalSpring have their own convention: see the description of each method."
  ],
  "fields": {},
  "functions": {
    "freqGenC": {
      "desc": "Cosine generator: cos(2*pi*t/period) * ampl. Useful for test signals.",
      "params": {
        "period": {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "period in seconds (1e-30 added to avoid division by zero)"
        },
        "ampl": {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "amplitude"
        },
        "t": {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "time in seconds"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "signal value"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newFreqFilter1": {
      "desc": "Creates a first-order filter (low-pass, high-pass, band-pass, band-stop), with internal state. Each method is called once per step with the new sample.",
      "params": {},
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "freqFilter1",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newFreqDetector": {
      "desc": "Creates a frequency detector for an oscillating signal (tracks peaks and troughs). See the freqDetector class.",
      "params": {},
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "freqDetector",
          "desc": "detector"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newFreqExists": {
      "desc": "Creates an amplitude detector at a target frequency (Goertzel algorithm). See the freqExists class.",
      "params": {},
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "freqExists",
          "desc": "detector"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newTemporalSpring": {
      "desc": "Creates a damped spring filter that follows the setpoint (smoothed value with velocity and inertia).",
      "params": {
        "spring": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "stiffness, default 10"
        },
        "damp": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "damping, default 2"
        },
        "startingValue": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial value, default 0"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "temporalSpring",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newTemporalSigmoidSmoothing": {
      "desc": "Creates an S-curve smoothing (acceleration limited at start and stop, speed bounded by the rate). Less abrupt than linear smoothing.",
      "params": {
        "inRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "max speed (units/s), default 1"
        },
        "startAccel": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "start acceleration, default +infinity"
        },
        "stopAccel": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "arrival deceleration, default startAccel"
        },
        "outRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "max speed when the value moves away from 0 (key true), default inRate"
        },
        "startingValue": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial value, default 0"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "temporalSigmoidSmoothing",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newTemporalSmoothingHybrid": {
      "desc": "Creates an exponential smoothing with a linear minimum speed (avoids the infinite tail of the exponential).",
      "params": {
        "inRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "exponential rate (1/s), default 1, capped at 1e30"
        },
        "outRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "rate when the difference has the same sign as the state, default inRate"
        },
        "startingValue": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial value, default 0"
        },
        "linearRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "minimum speed (units/s), default 0"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "temporalSmoothingHybrid",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newTemporalSmoothingNonLinear": {
      "desc": "Creates a pure exponential smoothing: st += (sample - st) * r/(1+r) with r = rate*dt.",
      "params": {
        "inRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "rate (1/s), default 1, capped at 1e30"
        },
        "outRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "rate when the difference has the same sign as the state, default inRate"
        },
        "startingValue": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial value, default 0"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "temporalSmoothingNonLinear",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newTemporalSmoothing": {
      "desc": "Creates a linear smoothing over time (the value moves at a bounded speed toward the setpoint). Typical for pedals, steering. Can have an auto-centering rate when the setpoint is exactly 0.",
      "params": {
        "inRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "speed (units/s) when the value comes back toward 0, default 1, min 1e-307"
        },
        "outRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "speed when it moves away from 0, default inRate"
        },
        "autoCenterRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "auto-centering speed when sample == 0, default inRate"
        },
        "startingValue": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial value (also reset value), default 0"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "temporalSmoothing",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newLinearSmoothing": {
      "desc": "Creates a linear smoothing with a FIXED time step dt (get does not take dt); no auto-centering.",
      "params": {
        "dt": {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "fixed time step in seconds"
        },
        "inRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "speed when the value comes back toward 0, default 1"
        },
        "outRate": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "speed when it moves away from 0, default inRate"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "linearSmoothing",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newNopSmoothing": {
      "desc": "Neutral filter: get(sample) returns sample. Used to disable a smoothing without changing the calling code.",
      "params": {},
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "nopSmoothing",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newExponentialSmoothing": {
      "desc": "Creates a fixed-step exponential average, parameterized by a window in number of samples (minimum 2).",
      "params": {
        "window": {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "window in samples"
        },
        "startingValue": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial value, default 0"
        },
        "fixedDt": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "reference time step, default 0.0005 s"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "exponentialSmoothing",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newExponentialSmoothingT": {
      "desc": "Creates an exponential average with trend tracking (reduces lag on ramps); window2 sets the trend memory.",
      "params": {
        "window": {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "window in samples (min 2)"
        },
        "window2": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "trend window, default infinite"
        },
        "startingValue": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial value, default 0"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "exponentialSmoothingT",
          "desc": "filter"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    },
    "newLineFitting": {
      "desc": "Creates an estimator of the line y = weight*x + bias by exponentially weighted least squares (recursive update). Scale the inputs to [0,1] or [-1,1] for stability.",
      "params": {
        "window": {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "memory: in samples (getS) or in seconds (get)"
        },
        "weight": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial slope, default 0"
        },
        "bias": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initial intercept, default 0"
        },
        "scale": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "initialization scale of the covariance matrix, default 1000"
        },
        "weightMin": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "slope lower bound"
        },
        "weightMax": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "slope upper bound"
        },
        "biasMin": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "intercept lower bound"
        },
        "biasMax": {
          "type": "number|nil",
          "desc": "intercept upper bound"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "lineFitting",
          "desc": "estimator"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    }
  },
